  "description": "If you grow your own summer squash, belong to a CSA, or just shop at a farmers market, the weekly haul of zucchini and corn can be overwhelming. Our solution? Shred it, squeeze it, mix it into a cheesy batter, and fritter it away. Literally. Next thing you know, you'll be wanting even more.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 1 anchovy fillet, finely minced (optional; omit to keep the dish vegetarian)\n\nOptional substitutions: sour cream → Greek yogurt; zucchini squash → summer squash; shredded Gruyère cheese → cheddar cheese; Olive oil → vegetable oil",
